  "item": 373,
  "proof_object": {
    "actual_U": "Therefore U_11=gcd(Q^[1],rad_{>A}(S_sym)) exactly. This is a prime-independent actual-family formula, but log S_sym is at most 2N log A=(2+o(1))log b and gives no new capacity bound.",
    "bounded_degree": "For F=P*C(E)/V with V a p-unit, an extra p is equivalent to p|C(E). For a first-quotient residual H=C(E)/D with D and the coefficients bounded by b^o, positive beta mass gives E>A^(r-1) with r=Omega(n). A nonconstant fixed-degree C then satisfies |H|>=E^d/(2D), so it is not sub-beta. The constant/content branch needs a new actual divisibility theorem.",
    "first_quotient": "At a singleton hit j, v_p(P)=1, E is a unit, and (P/p)E^{-1}=Z_j/p mod p with 1<=Z_j/p<A. Thus P, P*E^r, and their p-unit monomial quotients have exact valuation one.",
    "scope": "The theorem closes top-symmetric monomial/unit first quotients and sub-beta bounded-degree univariate C(E) portfolios. It does not close multivariate elementary-symmetric cancellations, gcd/radical height, or beta-height full-support states.",
    "symmetric_carrier": "For positive actual loads set P=product Z_j, E=sum_j P/Z_j, and S_sym=P/gcd(P,(|t|E)^N). Since p>A and Z_j<A^2 imply v_p(Z_j)<=1, S_sym has valuation one exactly at t-away singleton incidences and zero at all other p>A."
  },
  "proof_object_digest": "093173f8e447dc9b0dc369bb36acf4d8a0fa1a6da74bdc79416f0ca967691343",
